From: nwrt Xiaomi 14 Pro integration
Subject: [PATCH] qcom-soc: skip PDC on the in-SoC phone modem

Xiaomi's downstream shennong modem resets the QMI transport when generic
ModemManager enumerates every PDC software configuration during initial
probing.  The PDC service is only used for carrier firmware selection; it is
not required for registration, packet data, signal, SMS, or SIM management.

Skip allocating the optional PDC client only for the qcom-soc plugin.  Other
QMI devices retain the upstream service set and behaviour.

--- a/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c
@@ -13794,10 +13794,21 @@ allocate_next_client (GTask *task)
 {
+    MMBroadbandModemQmi          *self;
     InitializationStartedContext *ctx;
 
+    self = g_task_get_source_object (task);
     ctx = g_task_get_task_data (task);
 
+    /* The downstream Xiaomi phone modem drops the QRTR transport when PDC
+     * enumeration runs.  PDC is optional and unrelated to CPE data/SMS. */
+    while (ctx->service_index < G_N_ELEMENTS (qmi_services) &&
+           qmi_services[ctx->service_index] == QMI_SERVICE_PDC &&
+           g_strcmp0 (mm_base_modem_get_plugin (MM_BASE_MODEM (self)), "qcom-soc") == 0) {
+        mm_obj_dbg (self, "skipping optional PDC client on qcom-soc");
+        ctx->service_index++;
+    }
+
     if (ctx->service_index == G_N_ELEMENTS (qmi_services)) {
         parent_initialization_started (task);
         return;
